            "adapter": "frame/launcher-widget",
            "geometry": {
                "$comment": "The sizes are DISCRETE LAUNCHER GRID UNITS: each `label` is the cell count a design is authored at (`3x2`), and its dp the portrait size Android documents for that count, (73n - 16) x (118m - 16) dp (developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/appwidgets/layouts, measured on a Pixel 4's 5x4 grid). Real launchers vary the cell size, which is why the cell count is what a design states and this dp is its reference rendering. The same table is WidgetSize in widget-catalog/src/main/kotlin/ee/schimke/remotewidgets/WidgetSizes.kt and the breakpoints in catalog.spec.json; WidgetSizeTest holds all three together.",
